# Pipeline OS — Cursor side

Pipeline is the governance kernel. Cursor does not replace Codex/Claude
mailbox seats; it adopts the same durable-state habits.

## Startup (non-trivial work)

```bash
cd /Users/hyungkoookkim/Pipeline
env -u GIT_INDEX_FILE .venv/bin/python scripts/ci_smoke.py
env -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git log --oneline -5
env -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git status --short --branch
```

Default posture: readiness bridge / local builder. Escalate to a named seat
only when the user explicitly names one.

## Habits

- Durable state beats chat: git, mailbox, plans, tests, gate evidence.
- `env -u GIT_INDEX_FILE` for ordinary git and shared checks.
- Find definition, writers, callers, siblings before editing a symbol.
- Smallest sufficient verification; tests prove only what they execute.
- Push, merge, lock, mailbox publish, and spend need separate user authority.
- Do not start product work from `~/Content`.

## Cursor surfaces only

Cursor workflow lives under `.cursor/rules/` and
`docs/protocol/cursor/`. Do not rewrite Codex/Claude ledger bridges for
Cursor-only retargets.
